    "3.6",
    "Text document saved in the OpenDocument format, but stored as a flat XML file instead of the.ZIP container used by.ODT files; allows the document information to be more human readable; also provides an easier alternative than the ODT format for generating documents automatically without needing a document editor. NOTE: You can manually generate an FODT file from an ODT file using the oowriter command line utility: oowriter --convert-to fodt myDoc.odt. Windows OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Writer. LibreOfficeFree.",
