    ["text_files",
    ".SE",
    "Shuttle Document",
    "3.4",
    "File containing code written in the Shuttle language, a lightweight markup language that can be converted into HTML5. Some syntax rules include: Text is converted into blocks of text that are separated by a blank line A header begins with a #, with the number of #s preceding the header signifying the heading level number. Ordered lists use numbers with a period, while unordered lists just use hyphens. Links are inline [] () or reference [] [], while link definitions can be used anywhere in the document. One blank space is allowed between the two parts of the link. Images function the same as links but the syntax begins with an exclamation mark (!). Horizontal rules are created with three or more hyphens. NOTE: Shuttle converters are available for conversion to Java and PHP. Windows Any text editor Mac Any text editor Linux Any text editor.",
    "Windows Any text editor. Mac Any text editor. Linux Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["text_files",
    ".SAF",
    "SafeText File",
    "3.4",
    "Map file format used by DeLorme Street Atlas USA, a custom mapping and GPS navigation program; contains a detailed map of a specific region; also stores the map center coordinates, the current zoom level and magnification, user preferences, and custom routes or layers added by the user. SAF files are saved by default in the C:/DeLorme Docs/Map Files directory. NOTE: DeLorme discontinued Street Atlas USA. Windows DeLorme Street Atlas USA. Copy-protected audio file format developed by InterTrust that incorporates DRM (digital rights management); used for downloading purchased music to MusicMatch Jukebox. Windows MusicMatch Jukebox. Password-protected text document that is encrypted so other people cannot read it. Windows SafeText. Locked archive created by McAfee Fortress data protection software, which has now been discontinued; stores a file using password protection and encryption; can only be opened with the McAfee Fortress software. Windows McAfee Fortress. An SAF file is a game data file used by EA Sports Cricket 07 or another EA Sports Cricket video game. It contains plain text information that defines how the game animates a cricket shot. Some modders edit and create custom copies of Crickets SAF files while modding the game. Cricket 07 is the last game in EA Sportss Cricket series of games. For this reason, it remains popular among cricket enthusiasts. Cricket 07 players have produced many mods and patches for the game, some of which depend on the games SAF files. For example, a modder who is trying to add a new shot to Cricket 07 may need to copy an existing SAF file and associate it with the shot, so the shot has an in-game animation. You can find Cricket players discussing SAF files and Cricket mods and patches in the forums on PlanetCricket.org. You can use BigGUI (Windows) to extract SAF files from EA Sports Cricket video games. You can then open and edit the files with any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows) or Apple TextEdit (Mac). Windows Cricket 07. BigGUI. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor Linux Vim. Any text editor.",
    "Windows DeLorme Street Atlas USA. Windows MusicMatch Jukebox. Windows SafeText. Windows McAfee Fortress. Windows Cricket 07. BigGUI. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor. Linux Vim. Any text editor.",
    "?"],
