    "3.3",
    "A DX file is a document created by DEC WPS Plus, a DOS word processing program. It contains a document saved in plain text. DX files can be opened by any text editor. DX files are very rare since the DEC WPS Plus program used to create them is no longer used, except for a few computer hobbyists. If you need to open a DX file, you can use a text editor. NOTE: DEC WPS stands for Digital Equipment Corporation Word Processing System. Windows DEC WPS Plus.",
