    ["text_files",
    ".PRT",
    "Crypt Edit Protected Text Format File",
    "2.5",
    "A PRT file is a part created by PTC Creo Parametric, which is part of the Creo CAD suite. It contains information used to record the parts structure and show it as a 3D model. Creo users often combine PRT files into Creo assembly (.ASM) files. Creo Parametric is a CAD program that engineers use to design manufactured parts and assemblies. Engineers can also use Creo to analyze the designs theyve created (e.g. test tolerances) and export the designs in formats used by Computer Numerical Control (CNC) machines. Parts created in Creo Parametric are saved as PRT files. While Creo is the primary application that uses PRT files, some other CAD applications can open them. NOTE: Creo Parametric was formerly known as Pro/Engineer and Wildfire. You can open a PRT file in PTC Creo (Windows) or Autodesk Fusion 360 (multiplatform). Note that you can open PRT files in only the Commerical version of Fusion 360; the Personal version does not support PRT files. All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows PTC Creo. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. Autodesk Fusion 360. Mac Autodesk Fusion 360. Linux PTC Creo. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360Free. Presentation template created by Corel Presentations, an application included with Corel WordPerfect Office; saves a slide style and layout that can be used for creating new.SHW presentations. Windows Corel Presentations 2021. CAD file created by CADKEY, a program used for designing 2D and 3D parts; contains both the model and drawing layouts; includes model geometry in wireframe, surface, and solids (ACIS based), plus dimensioning, annotation, vector, plane and other entity types in one modeling space. The Drawing Layout Mode in CADKEY contains defined views of model geometry for associative dimensioning and annotation, as well as section views. It also allows 2D wireframe geometry creation. NOTE: KeyCreator, the successor to CADKEY, uses.CKD files to store designs. Windows Kubotek CADKEY Kubotek Spectrum. A PRT file is a model part file saved in a three-dimensional model format used by Unigraphics, a 3D CAD program. It contains surface and solid information for a single part. PRT files are saved in a binary format, similar to an Alias wire model and an SDRC (Structural Dynamics Research Corporation) model. NOTE: Unigraphics was acquired by Siemens and is now distributed as Siemens NX. Windows Siemens NX Mac Siemens NX Linux Siemens NX. A PRT file contains portal information used by the Valve Visible Information Set (VVIS) command-line tool included with Hammer Editor, which is a program used to build maps for Valve games such as Half-Life. It stores a list of portals in ASCII format that are used by VVIS to perform visibility calculations to determine which objects on a map can be seen by a player and must be rendered. PRT file open in Apple TextEdit 1 PRT files are used to optimize maps/levels in Source engine games. The PRT files are generated by VBSP, which is a tool used to compile raw Valve Map.VMF files to the Binary Space Partition (BSP) format so that they can be used in BSP-based game engines. These.BSP maps must be completely sealed, meaning that they cannot connect to the black infinite area around the map. If the maps are not completely sealed, they will not work properly in the game. If the level is sealed, then VBSP creates a [mapname].prt file, which is then used by VVIS to calculate the visibility of objects and improve the performance of the map by communicating which objects must be rendered. If there is a leak in the map, then VBSP reports it and does not generate the PRT file, which causes VVIS to not perform the visibility calculations. NOTE: Since PRT files are saved in a text format, you can open them with a text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad or Apple TextEdit. However, you may have to change the.prt file extension to.txt to open it in the text editor. [mapname].prt - PRT files are named after the map/level for which they store portal information. An example of a PRT file name is d1_canals_06_d.prt. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. 3D model created with Solid Edge, a CAD program used primarily for creating industrial parts and assemblies; can be combined with other 3D parts in an assembly (.ASM) file. Windows Siemens Solid Edge. Contains configuration information that allows the computer to communicate with the printer; may be used by certain software programs, such as Dr. Halo software, which saves images in a device-independent format. Windows Referenced by the operating system. Output from a printing job sent to the printer and saved as a file; contains formatting information that tells the printer how the document should be printed. PRT files may be created on Unix systems using the FILEUTIL function with a Filename parameter. They can also be opened by FILEUTIL and printed using the LP (line printer) parameter. Windows Wasatch SoftRIP. Linux FILEUTIL. Protected text document created by Crypt Edit, a free program used for word processing; stores an encrypted and password protected document; may contain text, images, and page formatting information; used to securely store documents. NOTE: PolySoft Solutions discontinued development for Crypt Edit in 2000. Windows PolySoft Solutions Crypt Edit.",
    "All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows PTC Creo. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. Autodesk Fusion 360. Mac Autodesk Fusion 360. Linux PTC Creo. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360. Windows Corel Presentations 2021. Windows Kubotek CADKEY Kubotek Spectrum. Windows Siemens NX. Mac Siemens NX. Linux Siemens NX. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Windows Siemens Solid Edge. Windows Referenced by the operating system. Windows Wasatch SoftRIP. Linux FILEUTIL. Windows PolySoft Solutions Crypt Edit.",
    "You can use the Commercial version of Autodesk Fusion 360 to convert PRT files to the following formats (and some others):.F3D - Fusion 360 Archive.3MF - 3D Manufacturing File.IPT - Autodesk Inventor Part.FBX - Autodesk FBX Interchange File.OBJ - Wavefront 3D Object.SKP - SketchUp Document.STP - STEP 3D CAD File.STL - Stereolithography File.USDZ - Universal Scene Description Zipped."],
    ["text_files",
    ".FFT",
    "Final Form Text File",
    "2.5",
    "An FFT file is an audio filter used by Adobe Audition, an audio production application. It saves settings that limit audio frequencies so that certain portions of the waveform can be isolated or pronounced, including the sample type and Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) information. The FFT format is helpful for audio engineers since it allows them to fine-tune the sound of audio data. FFT file open in Adobe Audition 2023 Adobe Audition is a digital audio workstation (DAW) for producing professional audio productions, such as song tracks, podcasts, and video audio. It has various tools for creating, mixing, designing, and restoring audio with an advanced toolset. For example, one of the tools is the ability to reduce background and broadband noise on a track. To apply the noise reduction effect: Choose a range containing only noise (and at least a half second long) in the Waveform Editor Select Effects → Noise Reduction / Restoration → Capture Noise Print Choose the range you want to remove the noise from in the Editor panel Select Effects → Noise Reduction / Restoration → Noise Reduction (process) In the Effect - Noise Reduction window, you can choose Capture Noise Print, which saves a noise profile from the selected range so Audition can remove similar noise from the rest of the waveform. You can also save the noise print as an FFT file. To save a selected noise print as an FFT file, click the Save the current noise print option (save-to-disk icon) next to the Capture Noise Print option. You can only open an FFT file with Adobe Audition (multiplatform). To open an FFT file, select Effects → Noise Reduction / Restoration → Noise Reduction (process), then click the Load a noise print from disk option (folder icon) near the Capture Noise Print option. Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Final Form Text (FFT) document format created by IBM to format text that cannot be modified; includes document text as well as graphics data; used to fix the layout of document pages, headers, footers, and text. FFT files were commonly created by DisplayWrite, a once-popular IBM program used for word processing. Windows Corel WordPerfect 2021.",
    "Windows Adobe Audition 2023. Mac Adobe Audition 2023. Windows Corel WordPerfect 2021.",
    "?"],
