    "GIS file created for MrSID.SID raster images; contains georeferencing information that maps the raster image data in the SID file to real-world coordinates; contains the units of measurement for the image pixels as well as the coordinates of the upper-left hand pixel. SDW files are saved in a plain text format and may be viewed with a text editor. Windows ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Blue Marble Geographics Global Mapper. GDALFree. Text document created with StarOffice Writer 5.0 or earlier (also known as StarWriter); the word processor included with Sun Microsystems StarOffice suite; may also be opened with the Apache OpenOffice Writer program. StarWriter documents created with StarOffice 6 or later use the.SXW extension. NOTE: Apache OpenOffice was formerly known as OpenOffice.org. Windows OpenOffice Writer. LibreOffice. Mac OpenOffice Writer. Planamesa NeoOffice. LibreOffice. Linux OpenOffice Writer. LibreOfficeFree.",
