    ".VCT",
    "Visual Class Library Memo",
    "2.3",
    "GIS image created by IDRISI Taiga, a GIS application used for analyzing and visualizing geospatial images; stores vector data using connected points rather than raster data used by IDRISIs.RST files. VCT files are useful for storing mapped information such as roads and property boundaries. The vector data allows the features in the image to be zoomed without losing image quality. Windows Clark Labs TerrSet. Clark Labs Land Change Modeler. Safe Software FME Desktop. ESRI ArcGIS Pro. Blue Marble Geographics Global Mapper. Contains textual notes about a FoxPro visual class library (.VCX file). Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Project file created by VISE, an application used for creating Windows and Mac software installers; saves references to installation files as well as configuration parameters, scripts, and actions required to make the installation; can be built into a standard installer package. VISE is available in multiple editions: VISE X (Mac OS X), Installer VISE for Macintosh (Mac OS Classic and Mac OS X), and Installer VISE for Windows. Windows MindVision Installer VISE for Windows —  (Discontinued). Mac MindVision VISE X. MindVision Installer VISE for Macintosh —  (Discontinued).",
