    "2.3",
    "A XWP file is a text document created with Xerox Writer, one of the original word processing programs. It contains text added by the Xerox Writer user and saved in the Writer format. Xerox Writer was one of the first word processing applications released but is now discontinued. Windows Xerox Writer. Project created with XMLwriter; creates and validates XML documents and performs XSL transformations. Windows Wattle Software XMLwriter. Log file that records commands and events from a fax modem communications session; created by Intel Crosstalk Communicator, an early fax modem software program from Intel. Windows Intel Crosstalk Communicator.",
