    "Script used by Subtitle Workshop, a movie subtitle editor; saves a list of find/replace value pairs that replace optical character recognition (OCR) errors with corrected text; used for making the subtitle text more accurate; can be used for multiple languages. OCR scripts are written in a proprietary language that is similar to HTML. The scripts use regular expressions for text replacement. NOTE: You can view the pre-installed Subtitle Workshop OCR scripts in the /​URUSoft/​Subtitle Workshop/​OCR Scripts/​ directory. Windows URUSoft Subtitle WorkshopFree. Fax document received and converted to a standard text format; image data from the fax is converted to readable text using optical character recognition (OCR); created by FAXGrapper, an older fax program that is no longer developed. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS.",
