    ["text_files",
    ".WSD",
    "WordStar Document",
    "2.0",
    "Document created by WordStar, a word processing program for DOS used heavily in the 1980s; contains document data and page layout formatting; used to store text using the WYSIWYG DOS-based editor. WordStar is no longer developed, supported, or sold and is considered abandonware. However, Corel WordPerfect can still open WSD files (WordStar 2000 1.0 and later). Windows WordStar Corel WordPerfect 2021.",
    "Windows WordStar Corel WordPerfect 2021.",
    "?"],
    ["text_files",
    ".NWM",
    "Nisus Macro",
    "2.0",
    "An NWM file is a static or animated image that can be displayed on a Sony Network Walkman. The Network Walkman was an alternative to the iPod and other portable music players in the early 2000s. Models include the NW-E405, NW-E407, NW-E503, NW-E505, NW-E507, NW-A605, NW-A607, and NW-A608. An NWM image file can be transferred to a supported Walkman by following these instructions: Download / save the NWM file to your computer. Connect the Network Walkman to your PC with a USB cable. Open My Computer and you should see a new Removable Drive, most likely the E: Drive. Open the drive and look for a folder called NWWM-SCR. If the folder does not exist, create a new folder named NWWM-SCR. Copy the NWM file from your computer to the NWWM-SCR folder on the Network Walkman. (Only one file should be placed in the folder at a time.) Eject (or unmount) the Walkman in Windows, then disconnect it from your computer. Turn on the Network Walkman and hold the Search/Menu button until the menu is displayed. Select Display Screen and press the Play/Stop button to select the new display screen option. Windows View with an image viewer Transfer to a Sony Network Walkman via USB. Macro created by Nisus Writer Pro, a rich text word processor; contains code for the automated commands that take care of time-consuming tasks like removing repeated sentences or reorganizing the content of your table of contents in your document. NWM files are located in the following directory: ~/​Library/​Application Support/​Nisus Writer/​Macros You can also access pre-loaded NWM files by selecting Macro → Show Macros Folder in Finder and selecting the appropriate folder. To create a NWM file, select Macro → New Macro, add your content, and then select File → Save, name the file, choose the save location, select Nisus Macro from the File Format drop down menu, and click Save. To run the NWM file, select Macro → Run Macro from File.., navigate to the file, and select Run Macro. Mac Nisus Writer Pro.",
    "Windows View with an image viewer Transfer to a Sony Network Walkman via USB. Mac Nisus Writer Pro.",
    "?"],
