    ["text_files",
    ".BRX",
    "Beam Report Document",
    "2.0",
    "A BRX file is a deprecated application resource file used by older BREW 3.x and 4.x mobile application development programs. It contains descriptions of assets used by the application. The BRX format was replaced by the newer.CAR format. The Brew MP SDK replaced BREW as the latest development toolkit for the Brew mobile platform. The Brew MP SDK includes standalone programs as well as plug-ins for Eclipse, Microsoft Visual Studio, and Adobe Flash. NOTE: BRX files can be updated to the CAR format using the Brew MP SDK. Windows Qualcomm Brew MP SDK Mac Qualcomm Brew MP SDK Linux Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Document created by Beam Report, a word processing tool used to generate, merge, and post-process structured documents; contains document text and layout information as well as tags that label certain portions of the document with metadata; helps organize loosely structured information, such as meeting notes and general project information. Windows Systeam Beam Report.",
    "Windows Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Mac Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Linux Qualcomm Brew MP SDK. Windows Systeam Beam Report.",
    "?"],
    ["text_files",
    ".IIL",
    "CleanSweep Installation Log",
    "2.0",
    "An IIL file is a log file created by Norton CleanSweep, a program removal tool for Windows. It contains information about programs and files that CleanSweep scanned, altered, or removed. IIL files are plain text files, which you can open in any text editor. CleanSweep was a program that allowed users to monitor, compress, move, and uninstall programs. It was available as both a standalone product and as part of the Norton SystemWorks software suite. After scanning, altering, or removing a program, CleanSweep produced an IIL file, which recorded the actions it had taken. Users could review these logs to note what changes CleanSweep had made to a program, as well as any other information CleanSweep had noted about that program. You can open IIL files and view the CleanSweep logs they contain with Microsoft Notepad (Windows), Apple TextEdit (Mac), or any other text editor. Note that CleanSweep itself is discontinued. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor Windows Norton CleanSweep Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor Linux Vim. Any text editor.",
    "Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Any text editor. Windows Norton CleanSweep Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Any text editor. Linux Vim. Any text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["text_files",
    ".EMF",
    "Jasspa MicroEmacs Macro File",
    "1.9",
    "An EMF file is a vector graphic saved in the Enhanced Windows Metafile (EMF) format, an improved version of the Windows Metafile Format (.WMF). It stores 32-bit RGB image data in a series of records that are rendered on a display or output to a printer when processed. EMF file open in Adobe Illustrator 2020 EMF was developed and released in 1992 with Windows NT 3.1 to improve the WMF format, which was introduced in Windows 3.0 in 1990. Two of the main improvements over WMF are 1)support for 32-bit data (WMF is limited to 16-bit) and 2)its device-independence, meaning the graphic looks the same regardless of the device on which it is viewed. Microsoft later added this capability to the WMF format in Windows 2000. What is the Enhanced Windows Metafile (EMF) format? EMF is a vector format but also supports bitmap data. It can be scaled and output at a higher definition, which is especially useful when modifying graphics in an image editor and printing high-quality images. Image data contained in EMF files are stored in a sequence of metafile record structures. Each of these records stores drawing commands, object definitions, and configuration settings. Both the EMF and WMF formats are similar to the more common Scalable Vector Graphics (.SVG) and Encapsulated PostScript (.EPS) formats. Microsoft continues to revise the EMF and WMF formats. NOTE: Microsoft developed the.EMZ and.WMZ formats to reduce the file sizes of EMF and WMF files and make it easier to transfer the graphics between applications. These formats utilize gzip compression to compress the files. You can open EMF graphics with various image-editing and -viewing applications. Some programs include the Microsoft Office suite of applications (Windows and macOS), Adobe Illustrator (Windows and macOS), IrfanView (Windows), and XnViewMP (multiplatform). To open EMF graphics stored on your computer with Microsoft Word or PowerPoint, select the Insert tab, then click Pictures → This Device.. In Microsoft Excel, select the Insert tab, then click Illustrations → Pictures → This Device... Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Office 365. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2021. Corel Presentations 2021. IrfanView. XnViewMP. OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. CADSoftTools ABViewer. Mac Microsoft Office 365. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Cristallight WMF Converter Pro. Echo One File Juicer. OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. Planamesa NeoOffice. XnViewMP. Linux OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. XnViewMPFree. Macro file containing commands for automating tasks in the Jasspa release of MicroEmacs, an extendable text editor; used to automate repetitive tasks that would otherwise be very time consuming and monotonous to do by hand. Users can write custom macros and create new commands using Jasspa MicroEmacs extensive macro language then save them as EMF files. NOTE: EMF files are not compatible with other releases of MicroEmacs. mouse.emf - Mouse interaction macros. Windows Jasspa MicroEmacs. Mac Jasspa MicroEmacs. Linux Jasspa MicroEmacsFree.",
    "Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. Microsoft Office 365. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Newera Graphics Converter Pro. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2021. Corel Presentations 2021. IrfanView. XnViewMP. OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. CADSoftTools ABViewer. Mac Microsoft Office 365. Adobe Illustrator 2023. Cristallight WMF Converter Pro. Echo One File Juicer. OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. Planamesa NeoOffice. XnViewMP. Linux OpenOffice Draw. LibreOffice. XnViewMP. Windows Jasspa MicroEmacs. Mac Jasspa MicroEmacs. Linux Jasspa MicroEmacs.",
    "?"],
    ["text_files",
    ".WP5",
    "WordPerfect 5 Document",
    "1.9",
    "A WP5 file is a document created by version 5 of WordPerfect, a popular word processor. It typically contains formatted text, and it may also contain tables. The WP5 format was replaced by WordPerfect 6s.WP6 format. WordPerfect, now known as Corel WordPerfect, was initially released in 1979 for Data General minicomputers. In 1989, WordPerfect Corporation released version 5.1 of WordPerfect for DOS. This popular version of WordPerfect includes pull-down menus, the ability to generate print previews, and the ability to embed tables in documents. By default, WordPerfect 5.x saves users documents as WP5 files. WordPerfect 5.1+ can also save documents in the WP6 format. You can open a WP5 file with Corel WordPerfect (Windows). Current versions of WordPerfect still support the WP5 format. You can also open WP5 files with LibreOffice (multiplatform). Mac LibreOffice. Windows Corel WordPerfect 2021. LibreOffice. Linux LibreOfficeFree.",
    "Mac LibreOffice. Windows Corel WordPerfect 2021. LibreOffice. Linux LibreOffice.",
    "You can use Corel WordPerfect (Windows) or LibreOffice (multiplatform) to convert WP5 files to other formats. Because WordPerfect is the primary program that creates and uses WP5 files, it will give you the best results. WordPerfect can convert WP5 files to many formats, including:.DOCX,.DOC - Microsoft Word Document.PDF - Portable Document Format.HTML - Hypertext Markup Language.ODT - OpenDocument Text Document.RTF - Rich Text Format.TXT - Plain Text.EPUB - Open eBook.WSD - WordStar Document.WP - WordPerfect Document (Legacy)."],
